        <FormAndLineReferenceDesc>Part VI - Section B 10A</FormAndLineReferenceDesc>
        <ExplanationTxt>Active conference members constitute the decision making body of their conferences. Conferences are sectioned into District Councils headed by a duly elected president. A District Council represents 3-12 conferences. The Diocesan Council is composed of affiliated conference presidents and an elected Diocesan President. The board of directors of the council presidents (2 in the case of San Diego), in addition to appointed members (vice-president, treasurer, secretary). The appointed members should not exceed the number of district council presidents. Conference members direct their conference presidents to vote their desires and members direct their district presidents to vote their desires and represent issues on any issue of activity or governance. The Diocesan Presidents make up the voting membership of the National Council and they have authority to vote on issues and policies that affect the National Organization.Part V - Section B 12cThe presidents of the district councils will assure that all conference presidents and officers within their districts complete the Conflict of Interest questionnaire (Exhibit A) during the first month of their appointments. The questionnaire is updated annually. The Diocesan Council President ensures that the members of the board of directors complete the Conflict of Interest questionnaire.Part IX Line 24a - T-shirt &amp; candy used for fundraisingb - Equipment rental &amp; maintenance used for program servicesc - State &amp; Banking fees used for program services</ExplanationTxt>
